The text is given page by page; each page starts with its number, written [p. N]. The bibliography has been removed.

For each criterion, in the order above, give exactly one assessment:
- "met": the text shows the criterion is satisfied (for an exclusion criterion: that the reason for exclusion applies);
- "not_met": the text shows it is not;
- "cannot_tell": the text does not say.
Quote, in "evidence_quote", the exact words of the text your assessment rests on, copied as they are written (original language, at most about 40 words, within one page if you can), and give in "page" the number N of the page they are on. Leave both empty for "cannot_tell" when nothing applies. Never quote words that are not in the text, and never paraphrase inside a quote.

Then give:
- "decision": "include", "exclude" or "uncertain". Exclude only when at least one inclusion criterion is clearly not met or one exclusion criterion clearly applies. If an inclusion criterion cannot be told and no criterion is clearly failed, the decision is "uncertain".
- "inclusion_probability": the probability, from 0 to 1, that a careful reviewer applying these criteria would include this report.
- "rationale": two or three sentences naming the decisive criteria by their codes, written in the language identified by this ISO 639-1 code: {{ language }}.
- "decisive_criteria": the codes of the criteria that decide.

Reports may be written in any language: apply the criteria to their content.
